    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "it's not just a temporary thing though. it feels permanent. like the engine has actually died. i look at everything i used to love and i just feel like a parasite. i'm still eating, still breathing, but there's no spark, no purpose. it's like i'm just waiting for the world to realize i'm not really here anymore.",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Your sense of permanence might amplify the pain right now, but life often gives periods of stillness we mistake for permanent endings. That feeling of being a parasite can shift when you focus on one small, non-demanding task that doesn't require a big spark to execute. Remember that the person who used to feel full can grow back even when they don't feel like they have anything to give right now; healing is slow and doesn't always follow a heroic rush.",
      "source": "target",
