      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "It is completely understandable to wish you could stop struggling when the world feels so heavy and demanding. Many people find that accepting the present moment, even without the drive to \"fix\" it, offers a strange and necessary kind of rest. This doesn't mean your pain is wrong or that you must keep fighting, but simply acknowledging you are not ready to heal yet can sometimes feel lighter than pretending to be someone else.",
